##Practice_Q
How many customers with at least $100 spend on the store each employee is assigned to?
Here there are 3 tables:- employee, customer, invoice
employee(schemas):- employee_id, Last_name, First_name, title,...
customer(schemas):- customer_id, first_name, Last_name, company,...., support_rep_id
invoice(schemas):- invoice_id, customer_id, invoice_date, billing_address, billing_city,.., total

→ to find the solution we have to follow 3 steps
1- we have to find the number of customers for each employee
2- Then the customers who paid atleast $100 in the store
3-then the first one will be the main query and the second one will be the subquery in WHERE clause

1-to find the number of customers for each employee

SELECT 
  employee_id,
  last_name,
  count(distinct customer_id) as no_of_customers
FROM employee
Inner JOIN customer on
employee.employee_id = customer.support_rep_id
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 3 DESC;

2-To find which customer paid atleast $100 in the store

SELECT 
  customer_id,
  round(sum(total),2) as total
FROM customer
INNER JOIN invoice on
customer.customer_id = invoice.customer_id
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING sum(total) > 100
ORDER BY 2 DESC;

3-Now to get our needed result(actual query that we need to write-final query)
 Q:- Find the no of customers with  atleast $100 spend on the store each employee is assigned to ?

SELECT
  employee_id,
  last_name,
  count(distinct customer_id) as no_of_customers
FROM employee
INNER JOIN customer ON
employee.employee_id = customer.support_rep_id
where customer_id=
 (select
     customer_id,
     round(sum(total),2) as total
 from customer 
 inner join invoice on
 customer.customer_id = invoice.customer_id
 group by customer_id
 having sum(total) > 100)
group by 1,2
order by 3 DESC;

